            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0112" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.48/134a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-13T15:00:00-05:00">January 13, 1941—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. The American press has recently carried reports from France to the effect
                    that in view of serious food shortages in occupied France food supplies are
                    being sent from unoccupied territory, particularly to Paris.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph any information you may be able to obtain concerning the
                    authenticity of such reports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
